+## 3. Decisions and rationale
+1. **My own build of 1ef0646.** `node scripts/build-static.js --out <scratch>/qa-desktop-beta-4/dist` (7/7 beta
+   companies, 1 warning: Amazon's list is 6.76 MB), served by `scripts/cycle/serve.mjs` with a pid file. The live site
+   is not reachable from the sandbox; this is what Pages deployed.
+2. **Round-3 findings re-checked two ways:** their red tests (the round-3 groups `Beta desktop QA 3`, `Beta UX review
+   2`, `Beta viz review 2`, `beta a11y 2`) on this build, and one screenshot per finding at its repro
+   (`recheck.mjs`, `recheck2.mjs`). Phone-only UX findings (UX-39, UX-44, UX-46, UX-53, UX-54, UX-60) and V-46 are
+   the mobile QA's; their tests' results are recorded, not re-shot.
+3. **Card pay text for every paid posting** (`cards4.mjs`): `payPill`, `payHeadline` and `payLabels` lifted out of
+   `public/app.js` by name, with the app's own imports (palette.js, features/shared.js, features/roles.js) passed in,
+   run on all 23,509 paid big-tech postings. Every candidate was confirmed on screen.
+4. **D-46 is not a bug, by decision.** The lead (2026-10-17, on the 2026-10-16 decision): the card and the drawer
+   headline present every posted row ("we must present them as they are and not cut anything"); a row tied to no
+   listed place prices nothing only when a place is priced (`payAt`). Its red test became a guard that the rows are
+   listed and inside the card's range.
+5. **Tests read the build's own data.** Each `[D-n]` test finds its case in `getJobs` (or the served CSV) and asserts
+   on the screen, so it keeps testing the defect on a new crawl and passes once it is gone.
+6. **Severity.** Medium: wrong output a user acts on, in a supported state (D-49 the downloaded figures, D-52 the
+   Pay estimate). Low: a false or misleading line in one place, or a hard-to-reach control.
+7. **Load.** Other agents ran throughout (load average 4 to 30). The timing table was taken at load 6 to 7, the
+   quietest window; the timing tests in `npm test` failed at load 20 to 28 (§5).
+8. **Full e2e with my build as `dist`:** several suites read only `ROOT/dist`, so the worktree's `dist` is a symlink
+   to my build (never the shared checkout's `dist/`), and `BETA_QA_DIST` points at it too. The screenshots the suite
+   rewrites in `docs/screenshots/` are restored after.
+9. **Desktop Safari is not available here** (no macOS). Desktop results are Chromium 141 (Playwright); the WebKit
+   phone runs are the mobile QA's and webkit-phone.yml's.
