+#### D-52 (Medium): the Pay estimate for a city drops the city's postings that post one range
+- **Viewport:** 1440x900, light; the same at every width.
+- **Repro:** open `/melon-seek/beta/#c=apple&m=insights`; in Pay estimate set Level "Any level" and type "Software
+  Engineer"; note the estimate; then pick Location "Cupertino".
+- **Expected:** the estimate uses the board's similar postings that are posted for Cupertino: the 211 Apple postings in
+  Cupertino with pay and "Software Engineer" in their title, 184 of which post one range for all their places, plus
+  the per-place rows priced at Cupertino.
+- **Actual:** "Based on 38 similar roles at Apple, Cupertino" ($218K; any location: $214K from 500). Seattle: $242K
+  from 20, all "Senior … $175K–$325K" spans. Microsoft "Software Engineer": any location $177K (500); Redmond $188K
+  from 77, every listed comparable "Principal Software Engineer · Staff+ · 100% match", while 234 Redmond postings
+  have the title, 196 with one range; still "High confidence" and "Typically within ±8%". Amazon "Software Development
+  Engineer" in Seattle: 65 of 433. The "Most comparable roles" list also shows each posting's own headline range, not
+  the city's range the estimate used (Microsoft New York: estimate $231K, Low $188K, High $275K; listed "$120K–$235K").
+- **Cause:** `public/features/compstimate.js` `estimateComp`: a comparable is `local` only when it has per-place rows
+  that price the city (`p.rows ? payAtQuery(p, ql) : null`); with `LOCAL_MIN` (5) or more local ones, only those are
+  used (`comps = local`). A one-range posting that lists the city is never local, so it is cut. The list is
+  `comparables: comps.slice(0, 5).map((p) => p.job)`.
+- **Screenshots:** `D-52-apple-estimate-any-location-500-roles.png`, `D-52-apple-estimate-cupertino-38-roles.png`,
+  `D-52-microsoft-estimate-redmond-77-principal-roles.png`.
+- **Owner:** `public/features/compstimate.js` `estimateComp` (count a one-range posting whose places include the city
+  as local, priced at its range) and the comparables list (show `p.pay`).
+- **Test:** `[D-52]`.
